## 5. Valuation Procedures

### 5.1 Property Valuation Methods

1. **Comparative Market Analysis (CMA):** The Valuation Team will conduct a CMA to estimate property values based on similar properties in the area.
2. **Income Approach:** For income-generating properties, the Valuation Team will calculate the net operating income and apply a capitalization rate.
3. **Cost Approach:** Evaluating the cost to replace the property minus depreciation.

### 5.2 Annual Valuation Schedule

1. **Valuation Timeline:** All properties must undergo valuation at least once a year, during the first quarter of the fiscal year.
2. **Reporting:** Valuation reports must be submitted to the Finance Department by March 31 of each year.

### 5.3 Reporting Requirements

1. **Internal Reports:** Valuation results will be shared with the management team during quarterly meetings.
2. **External Reports:** Annual reports will be prepared for stakeholders, summarizing property performance and valuation changes.

